      "q": "How much federal contract money goes to Florida?",
      "a": "Florida has received $23.4B in federal contract obligations so far in FY2026 to date. The state recorded 158,484 awards with an average award size of $148K, and obligations fell down 27.8% year over year. Fiscal comparisons show previous totals of $32.5B in FY25 and $31.3B in FY24."
    },
    {
      "q": "Which agencies award the most contracts in Florida?",
      "a": "The Department of Defense is the largest awarding agency in Florida, obligating $16B in FY2026 to date. Other major buyers include the Department of Veterans Affairs at $2.5B and the General Services Administration at $1.5B, followed by the Department of Homeland Security at $1.1B and NASA at $653M."
